    "impact": {
      "type": "story-gallery",
      "blocks": {
        "pillar_product": {
          "type": "picture",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/tabi_grain_62_of_187_1.webp",
            "label": "Product",
            "caption": "A garment's value isn't determined by how green its label looks.\n\nIt's in the fabric you enjoy wearing, the fit you reach for again, the details you continue to appreciate, and the years of use it finds in your wardrobe.\n\nWe choose natural fabrics and explore craft and design with that longer relationship in mind.\n\nBecause the things we value are often the things we take better care of."
          }
        },
        "pillar_process": {
          "type": "picture",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Copy_of_VideoCapture_20250321-170744.jpg",
            "label": "Process",
            "caption": "We believe in making closer to demand and being accountable for what remains.\n\nMuch of our clothing is made after an order is placed, rather than producing large quantities in anticipation of sales.\n\nWe also find new uses for leftover fabrics through patchwork, smaller textile products and other upcycling initiatives.\n\nThere is always room to improve how we work. What matters is being willing to examine the process, not just admire the finished product."
          }
        },
        "pillar_people": {
          "type": "picture",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Copy_of_VideoCapture_20250321-124147.jpg",
            "label": "People",
            "caption": "Behind every garment is someone who knows how to make it.\n\nSomeone who understands the fabric, guides it through a sewing machine, finishes a seam, embroiders a flower or makes sure the final piece is ready to wear.\n\nWe believe their working environment should reflect the value of that skill.\n\nNatural daylight, clean and hygienic facilities, comfortable space between workstations, and wages that recognise their contribution are all part of how we operate.\n\nThese might sound like ordinary expectations. In 2026, they should be.\n\nFor us, the people who make Tabi are not simply a part of the production process. They are the people who make everything else possible."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "pillar_product",
        "pillar_process",
        "pillar_people"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Our impact",
        "heading": "A little more thought\nbehind what we make",
        "text": "<p>We believe the responsibility of making something extends beyond the finished product.</p><p>It matters what we make, how we make it, and the lives of the people who make it.</p><p>At Tabi, we think about this through three connected ideas: Product, Process and People.</p>",
        "text_font": "heading",
        "width": "medium",
        "text_align": "center",
        "text_align_mobile": "center",
        "list_label": "Product, Process and People",
