      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Upcycle by Tabi",
        "heading": "Giving fabric another life",
        "text": "<p>Making things inevitably leaves things behind.</p><p>And when you have spent a lifetime working with textiles, it becomes difficult to look at a piece of leftover fabric and see only waste.</p><p>Through Upcycle by Tabi, we've explored ways of giving fabric remnants a new purpose.</p><p>Some become patchwork and smaller textile pieces. Others are repurposed as filling for mattresses that find their way to families in our wider community.</p><p>A piece of fabric may have finished one journey, but that doesn't always mean it has nothing left to give.</p><p>It's a small but meaningful part of how we continue learning to make more responsibly.</p>",
        "text_font": "heading",
        "width": "medium",
        "text_align": "center",
        "text_align_mobile": "center",
